---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { labSamples } from '../../data/labSamples';
import { publicCrates } from '../../data/profile';
---
<Base lang="en" title="Technical lab | Miguel Quevedo" description="Public Rust crates with green GitHub Actions CI and standalone samples in C, Assembly, C++, Swift and PHP.">
  <main id="contenido" class="detail-main wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/en/">← Back to portfolio</a>
    <div class="detail-hero">
      <h1>Technical lab</h1>
      <p class="detail-lede">Standalone open-source repositories independent from Meson with green Ubuntu and Windows CI alongside isolated reproducible engineering samples.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lab-grid lab-grid--3">
      {publicCrates.map((crate) => (
        <article>
          <span class="lab-card-label">Public repository with green CI</span>
          <h2>{crate.en.title}</h2>
          <p>{crate.en.lead}</p>
          <p class="lab-stack-line">{crate.stack.join(' · ')} · {crate.en.status}</p>
          <div class="lab-links">
            <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href={crate.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open GitHub repo ↗</a>
            <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href={crate.ciUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Actions CI ↗</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="lab-section-head">
      <h2>Research &amp; Papers (9 technical reports)</h2>
      <span>Bilingual technical reports from Cockpit v2.1 and Meson with verified architecture, real test suites, and formal derivations</span>
    </div>
    <div class="lab-grid">
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Paper 1 · Technical Report v2.0 · Nov 2026</span>
        <h2>Cockpit v2.0: Native Multi-CLI Orchestrator</h2>
        <p>Native Rust + GPUI desktop orchestrator (~68k LOC, 52 runtime modules, 216 tests) and concurrent stdio MCP server unifying Claude Code, Codex CLI, Antigravity, and OpenCode. Measured v1.0 ablation: 94.13% skeleton reduction, 84.94% CLI filter, 88.34%–97.31% compaction, 3/3 LoopGuard (0 FP), plus v2.0 runtime expansion.</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">Rust · GPUI CE · MCP-Zero · LSP · 216 tests · 12 arXiv citations</p>
        <div class="lab-links">
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/lab/cockpit-paper/">Read paper (EN) ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/laboratorio/cockpit-paper/">Español ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/papers/cockpit-orchestrator-paper.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PDF v1.0 ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/projects/cockpit/">Case study ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Paper 2 · Technical Report v1.0 · Nov 2026</span>
        <h2>Zero-Vision Desktop, 3D &amp; Video Automation</h2>
        <p>Deterministic zero-vision-token MCP harnesses: Win32 UIA-first (<code>pc_ui_tree</code>/<code>pc_act</code>), Screenshot Diffing (&lt;0.15% unchanged / &lt;65% bbox crop), CPU Blender <code>bpy</code> (Quadriflow, PBR bake, R15 IK, 2×3 Contact Sheet = 1/6 frames), 10-rule Roblox Luau auditor + BFS, and non-destructive FFmpeg cut-lists.</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">Win32 UIA · Blender bpy · Roblox Rojo/Lune · FFmpeg · Python (~2.9k LOC)</p>
        <div class="lab-links">
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/lab/cockpit-zero-vision/">Read paper (EN) ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/laboratorio/cockpit-zero-vision/">Español ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Paper 3 · Technical Report v1.0 · Nov 2026</span>
        <h2>Local-First Multi-Device Agent Orchestration</h2>
        <p>Local-first network and security stack across Windows PC, Linux laptop, and Android: Hyper <code>/v1/*</code> HMAC-SHA256 API + OTP QR pairing, Iroh QUIC (<code>cockpit/p2p/1</code>), Tailscale Serve, app-scoped userspace WireGuard (<code>wgproxyrs</code>), <code>/offload</code> with <code>sysinfo</code> FIFO Resource Guard, and Kotlin 2.2.20 + ML Kit app.</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">Iroh QUIC · Tailscale · wgproxyrs · HMAC-SHA256 · Kotlin (~2.2k LOC)</p>
        <div class="lab-links">
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/lab/cockpit-distributed/">Read paper (EN) ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/laboratorio/cockpit-distributed/">Español ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Paper 4 · Theoretical Note v0.9 · Nov 2026</span>
        <h2>Algebraic Context Compression &amp; KV-Cache Laws</h2>
        <p>Formal derivations of multi-turn quadratic token cost and the KV-Cache Epoch Step-Function Law (<code>H* = 87</code> turns), speculative turn elimination (<code>τ* = 0.71%</code>), BPE hex fragmentation (<code>P_split = 0.46875</code>), Knaster-Tarski slicing, diagnostic <code>δ-CRDT</code>, absorbing Markov chains, and adaptive group testing.</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">KV-Cache Math · BPE Aliasing · Knaster-Tarski · Markov N=(I-Q)⁻¹ · Theoretical Note</p>
        <div class="lab-links">
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/lab/cockpit-algebraic-compression/">Read note (EN) ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/laboratorio/cockpit-algebraic-compression/">Español ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Paper 5 · Meson Technical Report v1.0 · Nov 2026</span>
        <h2>Offline-First Financial Apps, Double-Entry &amp; Fiscal Hash Chains</h2>
        <p>Mission-critical financial invariants: exact integer cent math via <code>BigInt</code> (<code>maxExact = 2⁵³−1</code>), immutable double-entry ledger, frozen multi-currency FX snapshots, 3-Way AP matching (PO↔GRN↔Invoice), blind Z-Close reconciliation, and SENIAT cryptographic fiscal hash chains.</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">ExactCentAmounts · Double-Entry · 3-Way AP · SENIAT Hash · 48 test files</p>
        <div class="lab-links">
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/lab/meson-finance-erp/">Read paper (EN) ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/laboratorio/meson-finance-erp/">Español ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Paper 6 · Meson Technical Report v1.0 · Nov 2026</span>
        <h2>Modular Multi-Tenant ERP, RBAC, BOM &amp; HR Kiosk Architecture</h2>
        <p>Governing 44 deferred-loaded modules (<code>deferred as</code>), operation-level RBAC guards, recursive BOM/yield/shrinkage/par-level math, Atelier HR attendance kiosk state machine &amp; payroll, hardware-bound HMAC anti-clock licensing, and RS-232 anti-theft scales.</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">44 Modules · RBAC · BOM/Shrinkage · Atelier HR · HMAC License · RS-232</p>
        <div class="lab-links">
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/lab/meson-management-erp/">Read paper (EN) ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/laboratorio/meson-management-erp/">Español ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Paper 7 · Meson Technical Report v1.0 · Nov 2026</span>
        <h2>Causal LAN Sync (HLC/CRDT/AEAD) &amp; Opportunistic Courier Mesh</h2>
        <p>Causal consistency during ISP outages: Hybrid Logical Clocks + tombstone LWW-CRDTs with anti-replay <code>ChaCha20-Poly1305</code> framing (<code>lan-delta-sync</code>), Isar WAL idempotency, and a DTN mesh relay where courier smartphones ferry encrypted POS deltas to the cloud.</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">HLC · LWW-CRDT · ChaCha20-Poly1305 · Isar WAL · DTN Mesh Relay · Green CI</p>
        <div class="lab-links">
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/lab/meson-offline-mesh/">Read paper (EN) ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/laboratorio/meson-offline-mesh/">Español ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Paper 8 · Meson Technical Report v1.0 · Nov 2026</span>
        <h2>Generational FFI Arenas, DAG Solver &amp; Zero-Cloud Edge AI in Rust</h2>
        <p>Panic-safe C-ABI / <code>dart:ffi</code> bridge with <code>u64</code> generational handles (<code>ffi-arena-bridge</code>, live C99 CI smoke test), incremental DAG spreadsheet solver with cycle detection, offline SQLite RAG + TF-IDF/SIF + Whisper STT, and <code>qbsdiff</code> binary delta patching.</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">u64 FFI Arena · catch_unwind · SheetDag · SQLite RAG · Whisper · qbsdiff</p>
        <div class="lab-links">
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/lab/meson-rust-edge/">Read paper (EN) ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/laboratorio/meson-rust-edge/">Español ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Paper 9 · Cockpit Technical Report v1.0 · Nov 2026</span>
        <h2>Power-Loss Crash Resilience, Git-Delta Resumption &amp; Fingerprinting</h2>
        <p>Split atomic persistence (<code>workspace_index.json</code> + <code>sessions/&lt;id&gt;.jsonl</code>) with 15s <code>sync_all()</code> durability against hard outages, <code>git status --short</code> delta resumption, CLI <code>interrupted</code> self-healing, and Black-Box Behavioral Fingerprinting (<code>ThinkingLoopGuard</code> + <code>ConsecutiveFailGuard</code> 2× FNV-1a + 7-class taxonomy).</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">sync_all() 15s · Git Delta Resume · Self-Healing · Behavioral Fingerprinting · $0 Tokens</p>
        <div class="lab-links">
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/lab/cockpit-resilience-fingerprinting/">Read paper (EN) ↗</a>
          <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/laboratorio/cockpit-resilience-fingerprinting/">Español ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="lab-grid" style="margin-top:24px;">
      <article>
        <span class="lab-card-label">Rust sample</span>
        <h2>Local synchronization</h2>
        <p>Vector clocks, concurrent changes and pending operations until acknowledgment. Five tests executed.</p>
        <p class="lab-stack-line">Rust · Verified</p>
        <div class="lab-links"><a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="/en/samples/local-sync/">View sample ↗</a></div>
      </article>
      {labSamples.map((sample) => (
        <article>
          <span class="lab-card-label">{sample.verified ? 'Verified' : 'Execution pending'}</span>
          <h2>{sample.en.title}</h2>
          <p>{sample.en.lead}</p>
          <p class="lab-stack-line">{sample.stack.join(' · ')}</p>
          <div class="lab-links"><a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href={`/en/samples/${sample.slug}/`}>View sample ↗</a></div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="lab-note"><strong>What this proves</strong><p>Alongside Meson architecture previews and live web deployments, these standalone repositories expose inspectable Rust, C99 shared-library FFI, Dart outbox/bindings, x64 Assembly, C++, PHP and Swift implementations with reproducible verification commands.</p></div>
  </main>
</Base>
